      {
        "id": 119808,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-30T17:45:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Matchstickman wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;arenson9 wrote:<br><blockquote>And still seems like a bug. Why should you get to change the choice?&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nBecause all bonuses are recalculated when redirection occurs.You look at all the cards and see which ones are applicable for this new target and apply them again/for the first time, choice of plus or minus 1 and type of damage are parts of the bonus that TtE applies.\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;You say this, and yet it still doesn't seem right to me. The reason many cards are reapplied after a redirection is because the target has changed and therefore which cards are relevant has changed. Twist the Ether is relevant regardless of the target, so I don't see why its affects would be reconsidered. Yes I can see how tactically it could be very helpful, but so what?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It is correct. It has already been confirmed by MigrantP that Christopher has said this is how it would work.</p>",
