      {
        "id": 119812,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-30T20:28:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Rabit wrote:</b><br><blockquote>For me, it's an issue of consistency.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nExactly, all or nothing.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The ruling is the ruling, so I'm no longer arguing how it should be played, BUT, the reason I don't find this consistent is that Twist the Ether affect's the source of dealt damage, not the target of dealt damage. If Legacy has out Fortitude and deals damage that is redirected, you don't have to check whether or not Fortitude is still in effect, because the source of the damage hasn't changed, just the target.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Edit: To be clear, I can see why y'all think of it as consistent – after a redirection, check <em>everything</em>. Just because Fortitude still applies doesn't mean it wasn't rechecked. I get that. I just saw Twist the Ether as something that wouldn't change. Christopher says that it does? So be it. I think, however, that what I described was just as consistent, albeit less simple.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:07.235Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
