      {
        "id": 119814,
        "name": "ctsdistrict",
        "username": "ctsdistrict",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/fbc32d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-31T16:40:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This is the order I use when determining damage:</p><p>Choose source of damage (One-shot, Power, etc.)</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Adjust damage with any global modifiers for damage dealt (Obsidian Field, etc.) I also normally keep track of global \"damage taken\" adjustments here for convenience.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Adjust damage based on source of damage (Galvanize, Imbued Fire, Twist the Ether</p><p>Choose target(s). For each target</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Redirect as needed</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Adjust damage based on target of damage (Damage reduction, Nemesis bonus)</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-If there is a \"next damage dealt\" adjustment, it goes here, then goes away for any further targets.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Target loses HP</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My personal opinion is that damage does not need to be micromanaged to a ridiculous level. I understand there is a large discussion of exact order and timing of damage operations. Like all \"unclear\" situations in Sentinels, ultimately the players may choose to interpret the order as they choose. If your group wants to argue about which modifier comes first or if you can use the same bonus more than once because of your special situation, more power to you, but we normally prefer not to take 5 minutes to decide on damage bonuses every time :)</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:07.371Z",
