        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-31T17:17:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Damage calulcations isn't unclear, <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/dealing-damage-timing-clarification-6047\">this</a> is how damage works.</p>\n<p>I did want to point out that your method actually doesn't follow the established rules.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ctsdistrict\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/fbc32d/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ctsdistrict:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp; -Adjust damage based on source of damage (Galvanize, Imbued Fire, Twist the Ether</p>\n<p>Choose target(s). For each target</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Redirect as needed</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp;-Adjust damage based on target of damage (Damage reduction, Nemesis bonus)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Redirect comes after all damage modifications, and those modifications can happen in any order regardless of source. However, you cannot redirect damage before taking into account the modifications of the target of the damage. If the target of the damage reduces the damage to 0 or fewer, you cannot redirect the damage.</p>\n<p>Here is an example of where redirect happens after all modifications: Mr. Fixer has Pipe Wrench and Driving mantis out. If the initial damage is 3, he can reduce that to 2, and then redirect it. If the initial damage is 1, it would be reduced to 0, and he can't redirect it.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:07.454Z",
